/*
We need count pairs (i, j), usually unordered pairs of distinct nodes,
such that rooted subtrees Ti and Tj are similar.

Two rooted trees are similar iff for every depth d (relative to subtree root),
the number of nodes at depth d is equal.

For each node u, define vector cnt_u where cnt_u[d] = number of nodes in subtree of u
at depth d from u. We need to group equal vectors.

Observation:
cnt_u = [1] + sum over children v of shift(cnt_v by 1).
Equivalently, if we store polynomial/hash:
H_u = sum_d cnt_u[d] * B^d
then
H_u = 1 + B * sum(H_v).

But equality of hashes alone is not enough because vectors of different lengths can collide
under modular arithmetic. We can use two 64-bit style hashes with random bases and also
track height. Since this is a programming contest problem, double modular hashing is safe.

Actually length/height matters because trailing zeros beyond height are irrelevant;
two different vectors of finite support cannot be equal if heights differ and hashes equal
only by collision. Double mod minimizes this risk.

DP:
height[u] = 1 + max(height[v]) over children, 0 for leaf.
hash[u] = 1 + B * sum(hash[v]) mod M.

Then key = (height[u], hash1[u], hash2[u]).
Why is this sufficient structurally for level counts?
Because polynomial exactly represents level counts:
sum_d cnt[d] B^d = 1 + B * sum_v sum_d cnt_v[d] B^d
= 1 + sum_v sum_d cnt_v[d] B^(d+1).
Coefficient at B^k is exactly number of nodes at depth k.
So equal vectors imply equal polynomial; with two mods we compare probabilistically.

Need iterative DFS for N possibly large.

Input format is not explicitly given. Most common for rooted tree:
N then for nodes 2..N parent[i].
We'll support that.

Count pairs in each group: c choose 2.
*/

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int N;
    if (!(cin >> N)) return 0;

    vector<vector<int>> children(N + 1);
    for (int i = 2; i <= N; ++i) {
        int p;
        cin >> p;
        children[p].push_back(i);
    }

    const long long M1 = 1000000007LL;
    const long long M2 = 1000000009LL;
    const long long B1 = 911382323LL;
    const long long B2 = 972663749LL;

    vector<int> height(N + 1, 0);
    vector<long long> h1(N + 1, 0), h2(N + 1, 0);

    vector<int> order;
    order.reserve(N);
    stack<int> st;
    st.push(1);
    while (!st.empty()) {
        int u = st.top();
        st.pop();
        order.push_back(u);
        for (int v : children[u]) st.push(v);
    }

    reverse(order.begin(), order.end());

    for (int u : order) {
        int mxh = 0;
        long long s1 = 0, s2 = 0;
        for (int v : children[u]) {
            mxh = max(mxh, height[v] + 1);
            s1 += h1[v];
            if (s1 >= M1) s1 -= M1;
            s2 += h2[v];
            if (s2 >= M2) s2 -= M2;
        }
        height[u] = mxh;
        h1[u] = (1 + (__int128)B1 * s1) % M1;
        h2[u] = (1 + (__int128)B2 * s2) % M2;
    }

    struct Key {
        int h;
        long long a, b;
        bool operator==(const Key& other) const {
            return h == other.h && a == other.a && b == other.b;
        }
    };
    struct Hasher {
        size_t operator()(const Key& k) const {
            size_t res = std::hash<int>()(k.h);
            res = res * 1315423911u + std::hash<long long>()(k.a);
            res = res * 1315423911u + std::hash<long long>()(k.b);
            return res;
        }
    };

    unordered_map<Key, long long, Hasher> freq;
    freq.reserve(N * 2);

    for (int u = 1; u <= N; ++u) {
        freq[{height[u], h1[u], h2[u]}]++;
    }

    long long ans = 0;
    for (auto &it : freq) {
        long long c = it.second;
        ans += c * (c - 1) / 2;
    }

    cout << ans << '\n';
    return 0;
}

