/*
We need count pairs (i, j), i < j, such that subtree rooted at i and subtree rooted at j
are similar, where similarity means:
for every depth d >= 0, the number of nodes in the subtree at depth d from the root of
that subtree is equal.

For each node u, define profile(u) = sequence:
cnt[0] = 1
cnt[1] = number of children of u
cnt[2] = number of grandchildren of u
...

Two subtrees are similar iff these sequences are identical.

Observation:
If children v1..vk of u have profiles P1..Pk, then profile(u) is determined by the multiset
of child profiles:
depth counts beyond 0 are sums of child depth counts shifted by 1.
Thus if we assign an ID to each distinct profile, then profile(u) depends only on the
multiset of child IDs.

So we can process bottom-up:
- leaf => empty multiset of child IDs
- for node u, gather child IDs, sort them, use that sorted list as a canonical key
- equal keys imply equal profiles

Why multiset of child profiles is sufficient:
For depth t>=1, number of nodes at depth t in u's subtree equals sum over children c of
(number of nodes at depth t-1 in c's subtree). If child profile IDs are same as multisets,
these sums match for all depths.

Algorithm:
1. Read parents of nodes 2..N.
2. Build children lists.
3. Traverse nodes in reverse order N..1 works if parent index < child? Not guaranteed.
   So do iterative DFS/BFS to get an order, then process reversed order.
4. For each node in postorder:
   - collect IDs of children
   - sort
   - use HashMap<Key, Integer> to intern this key into a unique profile ID
   - increment frequency of this profile ID
5. Answer = sum over profile IDs of freq choose 2.

Need efficient key for int[].
Use custom IntArrayKey with cached hash and equals by Arrays.equals.

Complexities:
Total size of all child lists = N-1.
Sorting child IDs for each node costs sum deg(u) log deg(u), acceptable.
*/

public class Main {
    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
            } while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);
            int sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }
            int val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }
    }

    static class IntArrayKey {
        final int[] a;
        final int hash;

        IntArrayKey(int[] a) {
            this.a = a;
            this.hash = Arrays.hashCode(a);
        }

        @Override
        public int hashCode() {
            return hash;
        }

        @Override
        public boolean equals(Object o) {
            if (!(o instanceof IntArrayKey)) return false;
            return Arrays.equals(a, ((IntArrayKey) o).a);
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);
        int N = fs.nextInt();

        int[] parent = new int[N + 1];
        int[] deg = new int[N + 1];
        for (int i = 2; i <= N; i++) {
            parent[i] = fs.nextInt();
            deg[parent[i]]++;
        }

        int[][] children = new int[N + 1][];
        for (int i = 1; i <= N; i++) children[i] = new int[deg[i]];
        int[] idx = new int[N + 1];
        for (int i = 2; i <= N; i++) {
            children[parent[i]][idx[parent[i]]++] = i;
        }

        // Build traversal order from root iteratively
        int[] order = new int[N];
        int sz = 0;
        int[] stack = new int[N];
        int top = 0;
        stack[top++] = 1;
        while (top > 0) {
            int u = stack[--top];
            order[sz++] = u;
            for (int v : children[u]) stack[top++] = v;
        }

        int[] id = new int[N + 1];
        HashMap<IntArrayKey, Integer> intern = new HashMap<>(N * 2);
        ArrayList<Integer> freqList = new ArrayList<>();
        freqList.add(0); // dummy for 0-index

        int nextId = 1;

        for (int t = N - 1; t >= 0; t--) {
            int u = order[t];
            int m = children[u].length;
            int[] childIds = new int[m];
            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) childIds[i] = id[children[u][i]];
            Arrays.sort(childIds);

            IntArrayKey key = new IntArrayKey(childIds);
            Integer got = intern.get(key);
            if (got == null) {
                got = nextId++;
                intern.put(key, got);
                freqList.add(0);
            }
            id[u] = got;
            freqList.set(got, freqList.get(got) + 1);
        }

        long ans = 0;
        for (int profileId = 1; profileId < freqList.size(); profileId++) {
            long f = freqList.get(profileId);
            ans += f * (f - 1) / 2;
        }

        System.out.println(ans);
    }
}
